"use strict";(self.webpackChunkdatabricks_monolith=self.webpackChunkdatabricks_monolith||[]).push([[6272],{706272:e=>{e.exports="# Source Routing\n\nThe `migrate-to-sdp` skill is source-pluggable. The Research, Generate, and\nValidate-Repair phase docs are source-agnostic; per-source knowledge lives under\n`references/sources/<source>/`.\n\n## Detect the source\n\nInspect the project root the user provided:\n\n| Marker                                | source_type |\n| ------------------------------------- | ----------- |\n| `dbt_project.yml` at the project root | `dbt`       |\n\nIf detection is ambiguous (no marker found, or multiple markers), ask the user which\nETL source this project is.\n\n## Source packs\n\n| source_type | Pack root                 | Status    |\n| ----------- | ------------------------- | --------- |\n| `dbt`       | `references/sources/dbt/` | Available |\n\nFuture source types (Snowflake, Informatica, Hive metastore, etc.) will appear here\nas additional rows. The contract for adding one:\n\n1. Create `references/sources/<source>/` containing:\n   - `overview.md` — what's in a project of this type, what files to read.\n   - `decision-rules.md` — source materialization concepts → SDP `sdp_type`.\n   - `conversion-rules.md` — source-specific syntax conversion (templating,\n     references, tests, etc.).\n   - `examples/<pattern>.md` — at least one worked example per common pattern.\n2. Add a detection marker row in the table above.\n3. Add a row to the source packs table above.\n4. Register the new files in `entry.ts`.\n\nThe phase docs (`research-phase.md`, `generate-phase.md`,\n`validate-repair-phase.md`), the IR schema, and the SDP syntax reference do not\nneed changes when adding a new source. If they do, that's a signal those concepts\nshould be promoted out of the source pack into the shared layer.\n\n## Files a source pack must provide\n\n| File                                   | Purpose                                                                                                                                                                                        |\n| -------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `sources/<source>/overview.md`         | Project structure, config files, how to enumerate nodes, what each kind of artifact is (model / snapshot / seed / macro / etc.).                                                               |\n| `sources/<source>/decision-rules.md`   | Mapping from source materialization concepts (DBT `incremental`, Snowflake CTAS, Informatica session type, etc.) to SDP `sdp_type` (`streaming_table`, `materialized_view`, `auto_cdc`, etc.). |\n| `sources/<source>/conversion-rules.md` | Source-specific syntax handling (templating, refs, sources, tests, packages, macro expansion).                                                                                                 |\n| `sources/<source>/examples/*.md`       | Worked end-to-end conversion examples per common pattern.                                                                                                                                      |\n"}}]);
